  "result": "I fixed the cross-tenant read. `findIssueById` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts` looked issues up by `issues.id` alone, with no organization filter. Every other issue query in that file applies `orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId)`, and this one now does too. An issue id from another organization now returns `null`, so `getIssue` reports it as not found.\n\n`getIssue` in the service, `GET /api/issues/[issueId]`, and the update, status-change, assign and archive paths all fetch the issue through this function. The `assertOrgScope` calls didn't catch the leak, because they compare the actor's own org with the org id passed in, not with the fetched row's org. I checked the label, comment and attachment repositories and they were already scoped.\n\nThe issue-repository and tenant-scope tests pass. I didn't add a new test for the cross-org lookup.",
